# Tecsidel NMS - Technology Stack Documentation

This document serves as a reference for all the major technologies, libraries, and frameworks we are using to build the Tecsidel Network Management System (NMS).

## Frontend (User Interface)

The frontend is built as a single-page application (SPA) focused on high performance, modern aesthetics (glassmorphism, dark mode), and real-time data visualization.

### Core Frameworks
- **React (v19)**: The core UI library used for building component-based user interfaces.
- **TypeScript**: Used strictly across the entire frontend for type safety and catching errors before runtime.
- **Vite (v8)**: The incredibly fast build tool and development server powering the frontend.
- **React Router DOM (v7)**: Handles client-side routing (e.g., `/dashboard`, `/login`, `/monitoring/alerts`) without reloading the page.

### Styling & UI
- **Tailwind CSS (v4)**: The utility-first CSS framework used for all styling. It allows us to rapidly build the custom UI without leaving the HTML/JSX.
- **Framer Motion**: Used for all the smooth animations, such as page transitions, modals sliding in, and micro-interactions (like the hover effects on cards).
- **Lucide React**: Our comprehensive icon library.
- **Radix UI Primitives**: Used for accessible, unstyled UI components (like Tabs, Select dropdowns, and Checkboxes) which we then style with Tailwind.
- **Tailwind Merge / Clsx**: Utilities used heavily in our `cn()` function to conditionally merge Tailwind classes safely without conflicts.

### Data Visualization & Layouts
- **ECharts (echarts-for-react)**: The powerful charting library used for the real-time Traffic and CPU/Memory graphs on the Dashboard.
- **Reactflow**: Used specifically for the interactive Network Topology maps, allowing drag-and-drop nodes and edge rendering.
- **React Grid Layout**: Powers the drag-and-drop widget layout on the Dashboard page.

### Real-time Communication
- **Socket.io-client**: Connects to the backend WebSocket server to receive live metric updates (like CPU/Memory polling) and instant alert notifications without having to manually refresh the page.

